decoder/ - host side (Python 3, standard library only)

psc_maps.py      the one grammar of epcmap.txt / regmap.txt (DESIGN 10.6), read here
                 and written by handoff/impl/mkmaps.py (G2 attempt 2)
psc_format.py    PSC format mirror of linux/include/linux/psc_format.h
                 (struct strings of DESIGN 10.2/10.3, offset tables, flag and
                 sentinel constants). `python3 psc_format.py` runs its self-test.
check_format.py  cross-checks the C header against psc_format.py; exit 0 = agree.
                 `--cc` also compiles a layout probe with mipsel gcc 4.2.1 in the
                 build container (userland and kernel mode) and the header CRC
                 against zlib. Last output: check_format.out.
layout/          generated by check_format.py --cc (probe sources, .s, objects).

pscdec.py        the decoder of DESIGN section 10 (CLI, outputs, REPORT.md)
pscdec_parse.py  10.2-10.4: chunks, nonce CRC, run selection, confirmed extent,
                 (ring, seq) merge and conflicts, --raw scan, raw-image rule
pscdec_analysis.py 10.1, 10.3, 10.5-10.7: links, time, EPC/register maps,
                 template, per-poll simulation, onset candidates, 6.3
                 placements, every section 6 / 6.1 row, steps 7 and 8
synth.py         synthetic streams (healthy, H1-H10, none) for the tests;
                 built from psc_format.py, independent of the decoder
test/run_tests.py  the decoder tests; output in TESTS.txt

Decode a run:
  python3 pscdec.py -o OUT --build BUILD_DIR --times times.txt PSCLOG/
  python3 pscdec.py -o OUT --build BUILD_DIR --times times.txt --raw stick.img PSCLOG/
BUILD_DIR is the packaged build's BUILD directory (handoff/impl/mkmaps.py;
deploy/uClinux_TRACE/BUILD): System.map, epcmap.txt, regmap.txt, build_id.txt,
IMAGE.sha256, panellayout.txt, vmlinux of the exact image that ran.
Stage 3 closure (DESIGN 18, K3): the EPC analysis is refused unless
BUILD/SHA256SUMS verifies and BUILD/IMAGE.sha256 names the released image
4f9b69dc...cac8 (the G3 R3 record); --expect-image SHA256 sets another image
(the tests use the synthetic one), --expect-image any disables the check and
REPORT.md says so. Exit 0 = final REPORT.md; 3 = RAW IMAGE
REQUIRED (REPORT-NOT-FINAL.md only); 2 = inputs refused (e.g. one run number
with two nonces: choose --nonce). Inputs are opened read-only.

Notes and the rule-to-function map: handoff/impl/IMPLEMENTATION-decoder.md
